NVIDIA driver userspace, packaged for Basalt OS (basalt-nonfree repository)

These files come unmodified from NVIDIA's official Linux driver package:

  NVIDIA-Linux-x86_64-@VERSION@.run
  https://download.nvidia.com/XFree86/Linux-x86_64/@VERSION@/
  SHA-256 @RUN_SHA256@

Every NVIDIA file is byte-identical to the same file in that package: no
stripping, patching, relinking or compression. Repackaging into RPMs only
puts them in the places NVIDIA's own installer uses. They are distributed
under the NVIDIA Driver License Agreement in LICENSE next to this file;
using them means accepting it. GeForce and Titan software is not licensed
for datacenter deployment (section 2.8 of the Agreement).

Packaged by OpenBasalt for Basalt OS, not supported by NVIDIA. Report
problems with this packaging to the Basalt OS project, not to NVIDIA:
https://github.com/basalt-os/basalt-os/issues

NVIDIA, GeForce and CUDA are trademarks of NVIDIA Corporation.
